<title>NEW ZEALAND: TABLE-NZ ADRs end stronger on Friday, Dow settles.</title>
<headline>TABLE-NZ ADRs end stronger on Friday, Dow settles.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs ended last week on a stronger note while the Dow settled to close just 3.49 points lower at 8,113.44.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S. and</p>
<p>Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$28/03	  +0/01</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$32 1/4	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$22 1/4	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$12/15	  +0/03</p>
<p>MAS Tech	 NASDAQ  US$20	     +2 1/8</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$39 7/8	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$3.50		+3</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.89		+1</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  untraded</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of eight shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
